# ===== ARC-0020 stage 3 — Tier III "the lie explodes" (DV21) and Grand Deception reads the Veil (DV22) =====
# Tasks 0.6 and 0.7. Goal side: 42_goal_tier3_grand.pl (same stage). Numbers from 25: Splinter tier3_radius_next 4 m,
# Grand Deception doubles_range_next 3 m and doubt_per_double_next 1.
#
# Tier III, one burst per Splinter (review focus 4): below Tier III the Double's Splinter keeps its own 3 m damage;
# at Tier III that damage is switched off in the shout and the goal makes the burst with
# CreateExplosionAtPosition(Projectile_Deceiver_Double_SplinterBurst, 4 m) — for a Splinter cast (own turn, on
# Command, The Veil Lifts) and for a Double destroyed by an enemy. Pattern: vanilla Death Burst (GLO_CombatNPCs.txt);
# the projectile copies the mod's proven explosion Projectile_Arcana_Distortion_Explosion.
# The burst carries no ARCANA_IS_SPELL marker, like today's Splinter, so it never bursts a Seed.
# Retired, not deleted: Arcana_Passive_Aspect_Empress_Awakened_III_Damage leaves the Tier III status; the entry goes to
# 90_ARCHIVE in stage 5 with the Charisma boost.

@file Passive
@set Arcana_Passive_Aspect_Empress_Awakened_III Boosts UnlockSpell(Shout_Arcana_Card_Passive_WhichOne);
@set Arcana_Passive_Aspect_Empress_III DescriptionParams Distance(4)

@file Status_BOOST
@set ASPECT_AWAKENED_EMPRESS_III Passives Arcana_Passive_Aspect_Empress_Awakened_III
@set ASPECT_AWAKENED_EMPRESS_III DescriptionParams Distance(6);Distance(4)

@file Spell_Shout
@set Shout_Deceiver_Double_Shatter SpellProperties IF(not HasStatus('ASPECT_AWAKENED_EMPRESS_III',GetSummoner(context.Source))):DealDamage(1d6,Psychic,Magical);IF(not HasStatus('ASPECT_AWAKENED_EMPRESS_III',GetSummoner(context.Source))):ApplyStatus(DOUBT_ADD_TECH,100,0)

@file Spell_Projectile
@section Projectile_DECEIVER SPELLS
new entry "Projectile_Deceiver_Double_SplinterBurst"
type "SpellData"
data "SpellType" "Projectile"
using "Projectile_Arcana_Distortion_Explosion"
data "Level" ""
data "SpellSchool" "Illusion"
data "SpellProperties" "DealDamage(1d6,Psychic,Magical);ApplyStatus(DOUBT_ADD_TECH,100,0)"
data "AreaRadius" "4"
data "ExplodeRadius" "4"
data "TargetConditions" "Enemy() and Character() and not Dead()"
data "DisplayName" "{{h122c76dbgdcf9g6f07gcc55gacfcd3a5e30b}}"
data "VerbalIntent" "Damage"
data "DamageType" "Psychic"

@file Spell_Shout
@set Shout_Arcana_Card_Spell_GrandDeception TooltipStatusApply ApplyStatus(DOUBT_1,100,3)
@set Shout_Arcana_Card_Spell_GrandDeception ExtraDescriptionParams Distance(9);Distance(3)

# --- Texts (Narrative gate pending)
@loca hc6233dddg7b75g1f90g74acgcae8cb86d424 A Double destroyed by an enemy splinters by itself, and your <LSTag Type="Spell" Tooltip="Shout_Deceiver_Double_Shatter">Splinters</LSTag> reach [1]. You can use <LSTag Type="Spell" Tooltip="Shout_Arcana_Card_Passive_WhichOne">Ready: Which One?</LSTag> until combat ends.
@loca hb4946910g6b9agab74g91b3g4fd86b62a6b0 Veiled: Enemies with <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="DOUBT_1">Doubt</LSTag> have <LSTag Tooltip="Disadvantage">Disadvantage</LSTag> on <LSTag Tooltip="AttackRoll">Attack Rolls</LSTag> against you and your Doubles.<br><br>Two Pillars: Once per turn, when an enemy becomes <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="DELUDED">Deluded</LSTag>, the nearest enemy within [1] of it that carries no <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="SIGIL">Seed</LSTag> gains yours.<br><br>Aspect of Doubt: A Double destroyed by an enemy splinters by itself, your <LSTag Type="Spell" Tooltip="Shout_Deceiver_Double_Shatter">Splinters</LSTag> reach [2], and you can use <LSTag Type="Spell" Tooltip="Shout_Arcana_Card_Passive_WhichOne">Ready: Which One?</LSTag>.
@loca h0a59f46dgf3e2g782bg80d5g3ec6a72cd40e Surround yourself with Doubles until you reach your limit. Every nearby enemy that fails to see through the lie gains <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="DOUBT_1">Doubt</LSTag> for each of your Doubles already standing beside it.
@loca hb38d003bge7a3ge395gaf35gc74d0a5c2b52 Summons only the Doubles you are missing: you can keep 4, or 5 from level 12.<br><br>Enemies within [1] that fail a <LSTag Tooltip="SavingThrow">Wisdom Saving Throw</LSTag> gain 1 stack of Doubt for each of your Doubles that stood within [2] of them before the cast. A third stack leaves a creature <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="DELUDED">Deluded</LSTag>.
